**STEP 4. Assigning kinematic parameters, momentum transfer squared-\(t\) and azimuthal angle \(\phi\) to the selected elastic events.**

In this analysis step, we need to make use of the beam transport to calculate kinematic parameters, i.e. polar and azimuthal scattering angles \(\theta\) and \(\phi\) from the measured and selected positions of elastic events. In order to calculate the momentum transfer squared-\(t\), we first need to calculate the polar scattering angle \(\theta\) of the elastic events. The polar, azimuthal angles and momentum transfer squared-\(t\) are defined

