The uncertainty in the \(t\)-scale is mostly due to the beam angular divergence. To calculate how the uncertainty in the \(t\)-scale from the angular beam divergence we can start from using the expression for the momentum transfer squared \(t\), given in Eq. 167:

\[-t=p^{2}\theta^{2} \tag{185}\]

Taking the first derivative with respect to \(\theta\), the uncertainty on \(t\) due to beam angular divergence is then:

\[\delta(-t)=2p\times\sqrt{t}\times\delta(\theta) \tag{186}\]

where the beam momentum \(p=100.2\) GeV/\(c\) and \(\delta(\theta)=54\)\(\mu rad\) based on the study of the elastic event distributions \(\delta(\theta)\), calculated as a weighed average (all runs) of the \(\sigma\) of the \(\delta(\theta)\) distribution of each elastic arm, see Fig. 95. This gives a value for \(\delta(t)\) due to the beam angular divergence:

\[\delta(t)\approx 0.011\times\sqrt{t} \tag{187}\]

